Missing Vitest type augmentation. After `expect.extend({ toHaveLiveRegion })`, calling `expect(el).toHaveLiveRegion(...)` at every call site produces a TypeScript error (`Property 'toHaveLiveRegion' does not exist on type 'Assertion<HTMLElement>'`) because Vitest's generic `Assertion<T>` type has no knowledge of the new matcher. Add a module augmentation to this file so that the types follow the implementation wherever it is imported:
```ts
declare module 'vitest' {
  interface Assertion<R = any> {
    toHaveLiveRegion(options: LiveRegionMatcherOptions): R;
  }
  interface AsymmetricMatchersContaining {
    toHaveLiveRegion(options: LiveRegionMatcherOptions): any;
  }
}
```
This also benefits the companion test file, which calls the matcher without any `@ts-ignore` suppression.
